 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Totally normal. Want reassuring buddy along with you? Going somewhere you know well, like cafe, helps lot. Go up them all, order the main course you most want try. Stick to the basic versions if there are flavors you don't like. Then ask for a plate of sauces. Dressings are often the biggest offenders, and if you can taste the sauces first, you know what you' getting into. Most places have simple versions as starting points. Ask to skip the sauce you know you'll whine about, and try a little bit of the basic one. If it' a new style for you, and you' unsure, it gives you ideas that match your taste. Say you want taste of each style.",
